 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/De_SFrZPFae/",
 "title": "Negotiating Salary Based on Value Not Past Pay",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "This video discusses how to negotiate salary when HR objects to a large hike based on your current salary. The creator advises shifting the focus from your past pay to the value you will create in the new role.",
 "key_points": [
  "Do not negotiate your past salary, negotiate your value.",
  "Example script to use: \"I completely understand your concern, but my current CTC reflects my previous company's pay structure, not the value I can create in this role.\"",
  "Request HR to align the offer with current market standards and the responsibilities of the position.",
  "HR will often ask why you are worth the requested salary, so you must have a confident answer ready.",
  "Strong candidates do not negotiate based on what they used to earn; they negotiate based on the value they bring.",
  "Your last salary is your history and should not decide your future."
 ],
 "content": "HR says \"we can't give you 4x hike\" Your current CTC is 3.5 LPA and you are interviewing for a role that pays up to 15 LPA. Interview goes really well and then HR says we can't justify a 4x hike based on your current salary. So last week one of my student was in exactly the same situation and I told him that don't negotiate your past, negotiate your value. So he said, I completely understand your concern, but my current CTC reflects my previous company's pay structure, not the value I can create in this role. So I would request you that align this with the market standards and as also as per the responsibility of this position. So then I told him something else also, do not stop there, because HR is going to think a lot. Because HR will always ask like why do you think you are worth that salary? Even if they don't ask, but you should answer that. If you don't have a confident answer to that question, negotiation is already over. So strong candidates do not negotiate based on what they used to earn, they negotiate based on the value they bring. So your last salary is your history. It should not decide your future. Comment salary if you resonate with this. [Text on screen: Most Important HR Interview Questions & Answers! Are you preparing for a job interview? Do you feel nervous when HR asks questions? Don't worry! Here are some important HR interview questions you should prepare before attending your next interview. Tell me about yourself. Why should we hire you? What are your strengths and weaknesses? Why do you want to join our company? What are your salary expectations? Where do you see yourself in 5 years? Why should we select you over other candidates? Do you have any questions for us? Pro Tip: Don't memorize answers word by word. Understand the meaning, practice speaking confidently, and answer honestly! Save this post and practice these questions before your next interview. Comment HR QUESTIONS for more interview preparation tips! Share this post with your friends who are searching for jobs.]",
 "status": "done",
